                    "body": "Thanks for sharing! This indeed might be useful for future users.\r\n\r\nI'd suggest precomputing final size with `size = math.min(size, #projects)` and then use `for i = 1, size do` loop instead. This allows to avoid `if i > size then` check.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for sharing! This indeed might be useful for future users.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd suggest precomputing final size with <code class=\"notranslate\">size = math.min(size, #projects)</code> and then use <code class=\"notranslate\">for i = 1, size do</code> loop instead. This allows to avoid <code class=\"notranslate\">if i &gt; size then</code> check.</p>",
